@page "/docs/components/tooltip"
@using Blaizio.Docs.Examples.Tooltip
<PageTitle>Tooltip - Blaizio</PageTitle>

<div class="typeset typeset-docs space-y-10">
    <header class="docs-page-header space-y-2.5">
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
            <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">Tooltip</h1>
            <DocBadges Slug="tooltip" />
        </div>
        <p>Opens after a short delay on hover and immediately on keyboard focus. It is positioned against its trigger with <a class="font-medium text-foreground" href="https://floating-ui.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Floating UI</a>, so it flips to the opposite side when it runs out of room and always stays on screen. Inside a <code>BzTooltipProvider</code>, the delay is shared: once one tooltip has opened, moving to a neighboring trigger opens the next one without waiting again.</p>
    </header>

    <UsageBlock Example="typeof(TooltipDefaultExample)"
                Description="After importing `Blaizio.Ui`, a trigger and a content block are all you need. With `RenderAs`, any element can be the trigger." />

    <CompositionTree Root="Anatomy"
                     Description="Every part of a tooltip. The trigger and content sit under one `BzTooltip`, and an optional `BzTooltipArrow` goes inside the content. A `BzTooltipProvider` around a region shares the open delay across its triggers." />

    <section>
        <h2 data-toc class="scroll-mt-20">Portaling</h2>
        <p>While the tooltip is open, its content moves to the document body. That way no stacking context or overflow clip on an ancestor, such as a fixed sidebar, a transformed card or a scroll container, can cover or cut it off. Positioning, focus and dismissal work the same either way.</p>
        <p>Set <code>Inline="true"</code> to render the content in place instead. This helps under CSS containment, for print, or in tests that check the surrounding markup. Because portaled content sits outside your component's markup, selectors on its ancestors cannot reach it, so style it through its own <code>Class</code> or slot attributes.</p>
    </section>

    <ExamplesHeading />

    <Demo Title="Default" Description="Hover the trigger and the tooltip opens after a short delay. Focus it with the keyboard and it opens at once. There is no arrow unless you add one."
          Example="typeof(TooltipDefaultExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Custom trigger (RenderAs)" Description="The trigger renders a button by default. Use `RenderAs` when it should be your own element, such as the anchor here, and apply `p.Attributes` to it."
          Example="typeof(TooltipRenderAsTriggerExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Arrow" Description="Add a `BzTooltipArrow` inside the content to point at the trigger. It follows the side the tooltip actually opens on, including after a flip."
          Example="typeof(TooltipArrowExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Colors" Description="`Variant` sets the surface of the bubble: the inverted foreground default, the brand primary, a soft accent or a status color. A nested arrow always matches it."
          Example="typeof(TooltipColorsExample)" />

    <Demo Title="With keyboard shortcut" Description="Tooltip content is ordinary markup, so you can pair a label with a `Kbd`. Inside the bubble, the `Kbd` restyles itself to stay readable on the surface."
          Example="typeof(TooltipKbdExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Sides" Description="`Side` sets the preferred edge. When there is not enough room, the tooltip flips to the opposite side and the arrow follows."
          Example="typeof(TooltipSidesExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Shared delay across triggers" Description="Inside a `BzTooltipProvider`, once one tooltip has opened, moving to a neighboring trigger opens its tooltip right away instead of waiting through the delay again."
          Example="typeof(TooltipProviderExample)" />

    <Demo Title="No delay" Description="`DelayDuration` is the hover wait in milliseconds. Set it to 0 to open on hover at once. Keyboard focus always opens the tooltip immediately."
          Example="typeof(TooltipDelayExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Disabled trigger" Description="A disabled button fires no pointer events, so wrap it in a focusable span and make the span the trigger. The tooltip then still opens on hover and keyboard focus."
          Example="typeof(TooltipDisabledExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Customization" Description="Every part accepts `Class`. This example gives the bubble a brand-colored surface and a custom radius, and targets the arrow's slot so its triangle matches."
          Example="typeof(TooltipCustomExample)" />

    <Demo Title="RTL" Description="Inside a right-to-left `DirectionProvider`, the tooltip still positions against its trigger, and the layout of its content mirrors."
          Example="typeof(TooltipRtlExample)" />
</div>

@code {
    // The anatomy drawn by the Composition section - CompositionTree computes the connectors.
    private static readonly CompositionNode Anatomy = new("BzTooltipProvider",
        new CompositionNode("BzTooltip",
            new CompositionNode("BzTooltipTrigger"),
            new CompositionNode("BzTooltipContent",
                new CompositionNode("BzTooltipArrow"))));
}
